.TH BUFFER_SKIPSPACE 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
buffer_skipspace \- Skip whitespace characters in a buffer

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/buffer.h>

.IB int
.IB buffer_skipspace (buffer* b);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBbuffer_skipspace\fR function skips whitespace characters in a buffer. It takes a buffer as argument. The function skips whitespace characters in the buffer until a non-whitespace character is encountered or the buffer is exhausted.

The function takes the following parameter:
.IB buffer*
A pointer to the buffer structure.

The function returns the number of whitespace characters skipped.

The \fBbuffer_skipspace\fR function is intended to be used to skip whitespace characters in a buffer, such as when parsing text data.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBbuffer_skipspace\fR function to skip whitespace characters in a buffer:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/buffer.h>

int main() {
    buffer* b = buffer_new();
    buffer_add(b, "  Hello, World!", 13);

    int skipped = buffer_skipspace(b);

    printf("Skipped %d bytes\n", skipped);

    buffer_free(b);
    return 0;
}
.nef